WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:11.528 --> 00:00:13.534
- When Childish Gambino
released the music video

00:00:13.534 --> 00:00:16.540
for "Feels Like Summer," it
almost immediately hit the top

00:00:16.540 --> 00:00:18.626
of every trending page.

00:00:18.626 --> 00:00:21.836
The visuals show a cartoon
Gambino strolling down the street

00:00:21.836 --> 00:00:23.871
on a hazy summer day.

00:00:23.871 --> 00:00:26.874
Throughout the neighborhood,
63 different black artists

00:00:26.874 --> 00:00:31.411
and figureheads are in typical,
summer-related scenarios.

00:00:31.411 --> 00:00:33.372
Everyone on Twitter gave their thoughts

00:00:33.372 --> 00:00:35.832
on the different meanings
behind the video.

00:00:35.832 --> 00:00:38.227
We spoke with character
designer Justin Richburg

00:00:38.227 --> 00:00:42.270
and co-director Ivan Dixon to
see how it all came together.

00:00:42.270 --> 00:00:44.119
- [Justin] Part of my thing
is to make sure I capture

00:00:44.119 --> 00:00:47.260
everything as crystal clear as possible.

00:00:47.260 --> 00:00:49.060
- [Alana] Justin Richburg is an artist

00:00:49.060 --> 00:00:51.624
known for putting well-known
figures in unlikely

00:00:51.624 --> 00:00:54.874
and many times controversial scenarios.

00:00:58.182 --> 00:01:00.567
His black history month
piece, "Dice Games,"

00:01:00.567 --> 00:01:04.650
went viral and created
quite the reaction online.

00:01:08.065 --> 00:01:10.536
It also grabbed Gambino's attention,

00:01:10.536 --> 00:01:12.951
so much so that he put
the piece in an episode

00:01:12.951 --> 00:01:15.054
of his show, "Atlanta."

00:01:15.054 --> 00:01:17.355
- Like a week or so
later, after, you know,

00:01:17.355 --> 00:01:19.904
I quit my job, I made
the dice game picture

00:01:19.904 --> 00:01:22.475
and then it happened just
like that, that quickly.

00:01:22.475 --> 00:01:25.372
- So for that particular
photo that did go viral,

00:01:25.372 --> 00:01:28.515
you do, you know, create some
controversial stuff sometimes.

00:01:28.515 --> 00:01:31.546
- Yeah I mean that's on
purpose, because, you know,

00:01:31.546 --> 00:01:34.163
a lot of times when I talk
in regular life, you know,

00:01:34.163 --> 00:01:35.840
I offend people real easily.

00:01:35.840 --> 00:01:37.768
Might as well just put it in my artwork.

00:01:37.768 --> 00:01:39.645
- [Alana] How long did it
take, from start to finish,

00:01:39.645 --> 00:01:42.396
to sketch out 63 different celebrities?

00:01:42.396 --> 00:01:44.137
- [Justin] I think two months, maybe.

00:01:44.137 --> 00:01:45.807
- [Alana] Richburg did
say he wished he had

00:01:45.807 --> 00:01:48.648
a little more time perfecting
some of the characters,

00:01:48.648 --> 00:01:51.276
including Whitney Houston's curls.

00:01:51.276 --> 00:01:53.432
- With my style, doing
that type of curly hair

00:01:53.432 --> 00:01:56.241
is kinda difficult, like
you trying to keep it simple

00:01:56.241 --> 00:01:57.995
for the animators to copy.

00:01:57.995 --> 00:02:00.318
They kept on starting
over and over and over,

00:02:00.318 --> 00:02:02.841
and then like I'm trying
to get her eyes correct

00:02:02.841 --> 00:02:04.784
and all that, at the same
time trying to keep it simple

00:02:04.784 --> 00:02:07.489
as possible for them, you
know, to be able to mimic.

00:02:07.489 --> 00:02:09.550
- [Alana] Once the character
designs were created,

00:02:09.550 --> 00:02:12.206
the animation team then
began storyboarding

00:02:12.206 --> 00:02:14.061
based on Gambino's instructions.

00:02:14.061 --> 00:02:16.287
- [Ivan] It's a celebration of culture.

00:02:16.287 --> 00:02:19.647
Finished the video on the
Friday before it launched

00:02:19.647 --> 00:02:24.647
and we, that was like I was
compositing shots that day.

00:02:24.673 --> 00:02:27.534
So we never even got a
chance to watch it back,

00:02:27.534 --> 00:02:29.665
and do quality control, you know,

00:02:29.665 --> 00:02:32.240
we just delivered the
thing and it went live.

00:02:32.240 --> 00:02:35.132
So Donald already had a
pretty extensive brief.

00:02:35.132 --> 00:02:39.397
We were tasked with interpreting
the bullet-point brief

00:02:39.397 --> 00:02:40.537
into a storyboard.

00:02:40.537 --> 00:02:43.024
Justin designed 60-plus characters.

00:02:43.024 --> 00:02:45.252
- [Justin] I told them they
should do it like a "Bebe Kids"

00:02:45.252 --> 00:02:47.678
type of background, I
didn't wanna like, step over

00:02:47.678 --> 00:02:50.281
my boundaries, you know, I just
wanted to let you do enough

00:02:50.281 --> 00:02:52.549
and then let them do
what they needed to do.

00:02:52.549 --> 00:02:54.778
- [Alana] Gambino took
Ivan and the animation team

00:02:54.778 --> 00:02:56.511
through Atlanta's streets to get a feel

00:02:56.511 --> 00:02:58.440
of how the visuals should look.

00:02:58.440 --> 00:03:03.401
- We used Google Maps and
wandered the streets of Atlanta,

00:03:03.401 --> 00:03:05.761
trying to get, absorb as
much of the scant knowledge

00:03:05.761 --> 00:03:06.760
as we could.

00:03:09.590 --> 00:03:11.302
- [Ivan] Lyrically, my
interpretation of the song

00:03:11.302 --> 00:03:15.719
is that it's about global
warming and climate change.

00:03:32.150 --> 00:03:35.896
- That informed the color
choices of the background.

00:03:35.896 --> 00:03:37.623
Donald was pretty clear
he wanted it to feel

00:03:37.623 --> 00:03:39.077
hazy and polluted.

00:03:39.077 --> 00:03:42.494
Donald dictated the order of events.

00:03:42.494 --> 00:03:46.723
We only deviated a couple of
times for staging reasons,

00:03:46.723 --> 00:03:50.352
but he'd already paired up all
the people with each other.

00:03:50.352 --> 00:03:52.633
- While Dixon did say that
many of the situations

00:03:52.633 --> 00:03:55.634
that were storyboarded
were sheer coincidence,

00:03:55.634 --> 00:03:58.713
Gambino did get the final
say on the finished piece.

00:03:58.713 --> 00:04:02.041
And a couple of situations
definitely stood out,

00:04:02.041 --> 00:04:04.153
like the scene where
Travis Scott knocks down

00:04:04.153 --> 00:04:05.775
Nicki Minaj's blocks.

00:04:05.775 --> 00:04:08.390
Many have interpreted this
scene to be about Scott

00:04:08.390 --> 00:04:10.594
knocking Nicki out of the top spot

00:04:10.594 --> 00:04:12.155
of the Billboard 100 charts,

00:04:12.155 --> 00:04:14.808
and how Nicki was not here for it.

00:04:14.808 --> 00:04:16.670
- He didn't have the number one album,

00:04:16.670 --> 00:04:18.759
"Queen" was the number one album.

00:04:18.759 --> 00:04:20.107
- [Ivan] It takes a couple of weeks

00:04:20.107 --> 00:04:23.026
for it to be storyboarded,
designed, and animated,

00:04:23.026 --> 00:04:25.421
and we had already done
that before any of this

00:04:25.421 --> 00:04:27.095
latest conflict happened.

00:04:27.095 --> 00:04:28.339
Yeah, call it a premonition.

00:04:28.339 --> 00:04:30.210
Originally, the brief, I think it said

00:04:30.210 --> 00:04:32.684
they were playing Jenga,
but we had to drop that

00:04:32.684 --> 00:04:34.468
for legal reasons.

00:04:34.468 --> 00:04:37.626
Donald had indicated that he
wanted some of the characters

00:04:37.626 --> 00:04:40.984
to appear against a black
background during the chorus,

00:04:40.984 --> 00:04:44.879
we decided we'd have Donald
close his eyes and stop walking.

00:04:44.879 --> 00:04:48.215
I can't speak to his
decision for who appeared

00:04:48.215 --> 00:04:51.465
in that section, but we definitely knew

00:04:52.777 --> 00:04:54.919
there was like a somber kind of vibe,

00:04:54.919 --> 00:04:57.750
everyone had their eyes closed.

00:04:57.750 --> 00:04:59.395
- [Alana] Dixon and Richburg both say

00:04:59.395 --> 00:05:01.504
that there are a few
characters people online

00:05:01.504 --> 00:05:03.112
keep mixing up,

00:05:13.233 --> 00:05:15.150
and no, this isn't XXX.

00:05:17.330 --> 00:05:19.908
Did you catch any references
we might have missed?

00:05:19.908 --> 00:05:21.848
Let us know in the comments below

00:05:21.848 --> 00:05:24.348
and don't forget to subscribe.

